# summarize-github-pr

Show one pull request's metadata so a person can tell which PR it is and where its review stands. A script renders it, so it reads the same whichever agent shows it.

Run `scripts/summary.py <n>` by its full path from the skill directory, in the working directory: `gh` finds the repository from the checkout, or from `GH_REPO`. Under a sandbox that proxies network access, it reaches `api.github.com`. It prints markdown:

- a table of the PR's number and title, over its author and URL
- one bullet per review so far, with the reviewer, the review's type, and how many comments it started
- the PR's size, and the PR it is stacked on when its base is another open PR's branch

Print that output to the user exactly as it is, as markdown, in your reply. The script's output reaches only you, so the user sees the summary only when you print it. Don't add to it, reword it, or turn anything in it into a link. This skill describes nothing about what the PR changes, and changes nothing on GitHub.
